WHAT YOU DO
- Replace a word or a name with the posting's wording when it means the same thing (for example "ML Engineer" -> "AI Engineer", "containers" -> "Docker" only if that is what the text already describes).
- Insert a missing keyword or a short phrase (for example "with Docker") into the sentence where it truthfully belongs, only when the block already describes that work.
- Work in the listed items where they truthfully fit.
- Return a unit unchanged when nothing has to change in it. Returning the whole block unchanged is a normal and correct result.
{% if kind == "skills" %}

THIS IS A SKILLS BLOCK: a list of terms, not prose. You may put the terms most relevant to the posting first, rename a term to the posting's wording, and add terms from the items above. Do not delete a term unless it duplicates another one. Keep the same grouping and separators.
{% else %}

WHAT YOU NEVER DO
- Do not improve, shorten, expand, reorder or rephrase sentences for style, and do not strengthen verbs.
- Never remove or change numbers, metrics, names, dates or employers, and never add a claim, technology or achievement that the resume or the note does not support.
- Do not touch service words: work format (remote, hybrid, full-time), dates, locations and headings. Leave them exactly as they are.
- Do not add or remove units, bullets or list items. A paragraph stays a paragraph, a list keeps the same number of items.
- Do not repeat information the rest of the resume already covers just to fit an item in.
{% endif %}

OUTPUT RULES
- Return every unit with the same number n and the same type.
- Copy a unit or list item verbatim when nothing changes in it.
- Every item under "MUST STAY" must still be present.
- Plain text only: no markdown, no HTML other than the tags shown below.

OUTPUT FORMAT
Only the units, nothing else:

<el n="0">paragraph text</el>
<el n="1" list="true"><li>bullet</li><li>bullet</li></el>